      "notes": "PIN_LED / LED_BUILTIN - onboard general-purpose user LED. Confirmed via this board's own pins_arduino.h and upstream arduino-pico source; corroborated by absence from the official iLabs datasheet's external header pin table (Section 3.1), confirming it is a fixed onboard LED, not a header breakout pin. Active-high polarity is a cross-referenced inference: this board's own datasheet does not state the active level, but every other RP2040/RP2350 board audited in this family to date has been active-high (none active-low), and this board reuses the same iLabs Challenger product-line onboard-LED reference circuit whose sibling boards' own datasheets (e.g. challenger_rp2040_wifi) explicitly state \"Active level: High\".\nCheck if available on board"
